<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia merchandise imports rise in Jan.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia merchandise imports rise in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian merchandise imports rose six percent in January to A$6.792 billion seasonally adjusted from A$6.427 billion in December, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>This compares with seasonally adjusted imports of A$6.690 billion in January 1996.</p>
<p>In unadjusted terms, merchandise imports rose to A$6.402 billion in January from A$6.249 billion in December and compared to A$6.456 billion in January 1996.</p>
<p>Economists had on average forecast rise of around 2.0 percent in seasonally adjusted imports for January.  </p>
<p>    SEASONALLY ADJ	  Jan 97	Dec 96	Jan 96</p>
<p>    Merchandise imports  6.792 bln   6.427 bln   6.690 bln</p>
<p>    Consumption goods    1.732 bln   1.745 bln   1.634 bln</p>
<p>    Capital goods	  1.814 bln   1.410 bln   1.737 bln</p>
<p>    Intermediate goods   3.246 bln   3.272 bln   3.319 bln</p>
<p>UNADJUSTED</p>
<p>    Merchandise imports  6.402 bln   6.249 bln   6.456 bln</p>
<p>    Consumption goods    1.564 bln   1.732 bln   1.530 bln</p>
<p>    Capital goods	  1.558 bln   1.493 bln   1.564 bln</p>
<p>    Intermediate goods   3.280 bln   3.024 bln   3.362 bln</p>
</text>
